# ERP Software — Development Environment Setup

## Project Overview

This project is an ERP platform intended for ISO/API-style audit and compliance management. The initial development environment is being built locally on Windows, with the eventual production environment planned on Google Cloud Platform (GCP).

## Development Stack

- Frontend: Next.js
- Backend: NestJS
- ORM: Prisma ORM 7.9.1
- Database: PostgreSQL 18.6
- Production Database: Google Cloud SQL for PostgreSQL (planned)
- Cloud Platform: Google Cloud Platform (planned)
- Analytics: BigQuery (planned for future analytics/reporting needs)

---

## Project Architecture

The ERP application is structured as a modular full-stack system with a frontend, backend API, and database layer.

### High-Level Flow

```text
Next.js Frontend
      |
      v
NestJS Backend API
      |
      v
Prisma ORM
      |
      v
PostgreSQL Database (localhost:5432 / erp)
```

### Responsibilities

- Frontend: user interface and dashboard experience built with Next.js
- Backend: business logic, API endpoints, authentication flows, and service orchestration built with NestJS
- ORM: Prisma handles schema management, query generation, and database access abstraction
- Database: PostgreSQL stores ERP data locally during development and will later move to Cloud SQL in production

### Local Development Architecture

For local development, the project is currently using:

- Next.js app in the `frontend` folder
- NestJS app in the `backend` folder
- Prisma configuration connected to PostgreSQL on `localhost:5432`
- Database name: `erp`

This architecture is intended to support a future multi-tenant ERP platform for audit, compliance, CAPA, and operational management workflows.

---

## Initial Prisma Data Model Foundation

The initial schema has been defined and validated in both the root `prisma/schema.prisma` and the backend `backend/prisma/schema.prisma` locations.

### Core entities

- `Tenant`: client company, slug, subdomain, and tenant status
- `User`: tenant member identified by unique email, designation, and tenant-admin flag
- `Document`: tenant-scoped controlled document identity and current workflow status
- `DocumentVersion`: issue/revision content, effective date, review date, and procedure sections
- `WorkflowAssignment`: document-specific Prepared By, Reviewed By, or Approved By assignment
- `ApprovalDecision`: approval or return-for-correction decision with comments and timestamp
- `ComplianceReference`: standard, edition, clause, and requirement description
- `RevisionHistory`: page, revision, and change description
- `DocumentRelation`: links between procedures, work instructions, forms, and related documents
- `ChangeRequest`: controlled request to amend an approved document
- `PeriodicReview`: mandatory review evidence and next-review scheduling
- `FormTemplate` and `FormField`: blank Level 4 templates and their dynamic fields
- `QualityRecord`: completed data captured from a Level 4 template
- `FileAsset`: tenant-scoped PDF/image metadata and storage reference

The model keeps organizational designation separate from workflow assignment. A user may be a Departmental Head while being assigned as Prepared By for one document and Reviewed By for another.

The initial migration is located at:

```text
backend/prisma/migrations/20260820182439_init_document_control/migration.sql
```

It has been applied to the local PostgreSQL `erp` database. Future schema changes should use new named migrations rather than editing this migration.

Tenant isolation is represented through tenant ownership on users and documents, with unique document control numbers scoped to each tenant. The schema is validated, Prisma Client has been generated, and the initial migrations have been applied to the local database.

